{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"b91a19bb836e8ec6968ee4d8cc054eb60a4e600f39476f6291aa1522bdc2532a","packTokens":2810,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":215,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":273,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":616,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":1600,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nMap each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Import procurement PO and receiving data, map PO lines to lots and pens, and forecast lifecycle targets.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Track feed inventory, stock movements, forecasts, wastage, ration recipes, and ration costs.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Create pen-level feeding plans and log feeding activities, updating inventory and lot consumption and cost.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Record lot weight measurements and maintain weight histories.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Calculate feed-to-gain metrics and predictive sale/feeding insights, updating when feeding or weight events are recorded.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide operational dashboards, reports, filters, CSV/PDF exports, and yard-level summaries.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-7\",\n  \"text\": \"Create mock data and present the proposed solution, architecture, demo, testing, challenges, readiness, and go-to-market analysis.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"What user access model is required for operational and financial records?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use one shared access level for all users; do not distinguish permissions by role.\",\n  \"by\": \"Ahsan (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"When a pen contains multiple lots, how must a feeding plan allocate its planned quantity?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Require a quantity allocation to each lot and flag allocations that do not reconcile with the plan.\",\n  \"by\": \"Ahsan (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"How should the configured wastage ratio affect inventory decrements for an actual feeding event?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Decrement stock by the actual delivered quantity and apply wastage only to estimated consumption and forecasts.\",\n  \"by\": \"Ahsan (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"How should total lot weight be handled when a user records average weight and the number of animals weighed?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Calculate total measured weight as average weight multiplied by the number weighed; do not accept a conflicting independent total.\",\n  \"by\": \"Ahsan (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"What cost basis should the lot-level profitability analysis include?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Show feed cost per unit of weight gain using recorded feed costs only.\",\n  \"by\": \"Ahsan (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"How should users sign in, given that all users have the same access level?\",\n  \"answer\": \"No sign-in; anyone with the app link can access the shared workspace.\",\n  \"by\": \"Ahsan (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"When a pen contains multiple lots, how should an actual feeding quantity be attributed to those lots for lot-level consumption and cost metrics?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Allocate the actual quantity to lots in proportion to their planned quantities.\",\n  \"by\": \"Ahsan (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"Which ingredient cost should be used to calculate the cost of a saved feeding event when the ingredient's unit cost changes over time?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use the ingredient unit cost recorded when the feeding event is saved.\",\n  \"by\": \"Ahsan (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Provide the Feedlot web app as a shared workspace accessible from its app link without sign-in or role-specific controls, with all users seeing the same operational and financial controls.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Add mock procurement synchronization that requests PO and receiving records and displays returned fields, and support mapping PO lines to one or more lots and lots to pens with traceability, pen ID, capacity, and current animal count.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Display import duplicates, changed or conflicting records, returned conflict status and mapping information, and a review action.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Show each lot's target weight and projected market or ship date from returned forecast data, leaving the date empty for zero or negative ADG; display the applicable lot-specific target and gain assumption or configured yard target, including the same yard target for all lots when configured.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Provide feed inventory entry and views for item details and opening, received, consumed, and closing stock values; when a stock movement is refused for causing negative available inventory, show the returned error and shortage, keep the form available for correction, and do not show the movement as saved.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Allow users to configure a wastage ratio and view returned ingredient balance and shortage forecasts for daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, bi-annual, and annual horizons, marking periods without a dated feeding plan as unavailable.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Let users create and view rations with ingredients or as-fed proportions, nutrition and intended-animal details, and returned cost per pound; provide ration comparisons with returned costs and performance or cost-of-gain values and identify the lowest returned cost of gain when available.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"For inventory or ration screens showing ton-denominated prices, display the equivalent per-pound price in the configured currency and show calculation quantities in pounds.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Let users generate dated pen feeding plans from a selected ration, per-animal daily rate, animal count, date, and planned time, and display returned quantities, cost, energy intake, and status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"For feeding plans in pens containing multiple lots, require a planned quantity allocation for each lot and flag totals that do not reconcile with the plan; identify missing allocations and do not show an invalid plan as saved, while displaying the allocation field for single-lot pens.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"When a user saves an actual feeding event, display returned planned and delivered quantities, variance, feed cost, energy, inventory decrement, feeding status, lot allocation, and the ingredient unit-cost snapshot; show delivered-quantity inventory decrement separately from wastage-adjusted estimated consumption.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"Show planned-versus-actual feeding variance and provide an action and editable form to adjust a future plan for the selected pen and ration.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"Let users record dated lot weight measurements with number weighed, average weight, and notes; calculate total measured weight from average weight times number weighed, provide no independent total-weight entry, and display time-ordered history with returned gain since the prior measurement.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"When saved feeding or weight records are edited or voided, display returned revised balances and metrics while retaining the original record in history.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"Display returned lot feed-to-gain metrics, including days on feed, total gain, ADG, feed consumed, FCR, feed cost per unit of gain, and projected ship date, using recorded feed costs only for feed cost per unit of gain.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"After a feeding or weight event is saved, refresh returned lot metrics and display returned feeding-adjustment or sale-timing suggestions without requiring the user to re-enter the event.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"Provide an operational dashboard showing active lots and pens, animal counts, feed inventory status, ration usage, bunk rates, planned versus actual feed, feed consumption and cost, weights and gain, ADG, feed-to-gain ratio, cost per gain, energy consumed, and best- and worst-performing lots.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"Provide operational reports for the highest-feed-consuming pen, best feed-to-gain lot, highest-ADG lot, most-used ration, plan-versus-actual alignment, overfed or underfed pens, remaining inventory, and feed cost per unit of gain.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"Provide a Feed-to-Gain report with date-range, lot, breed, sex, and pen filters that displays matching lots' ADG, FCR, and cost of gain, and allow CSV and PDF exports containing results and selected scope.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"Provide a yard-level summary of aggregate total head, average ADG, average cost of gain, and total feed cost across active lots.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"Provide representative mock procurement, lot, pen, inventory, ration, feeding, and weight data, plus a presentation page with the proposed solution, architecture diagrams, demo walkthrough, coding prompts, testing and validation overview, challenges, production-readiness assessment, and go-to-market strategy and analysis.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"Render every page responsively for phone, tablet, and desktop browser widths, with touch-sized controls on narrow layouts.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}